# Node version for agent shells

Cursor’s agent shell prepends its bundled Node (`~/.cursor-server/.../node`, currently v20.x) ahead of nvm on `PATH`. Plain `node` / `npm` therefore hit the wrong runtime even though WSL/nvm has Node 24.

## Required before any node/npm command

Prefix every Shell invocation that runs `node`, `npm`, `npx`, `vite`, `vitest`, or project scripts:

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.12.0/bin:$PATH"
hash -r
```

Then verify once per session when relevant:

```bash
node -v   # must be v24.x, not v20.x
which node  # must be under ~/.nvm/versions/node/
```

## Do not

- Rely on bare `nvm use` alone — Cursor’s Node still wins on `PATH` unless nvm’s `bin` is prepended
- Downgrade Vite / tooling to match the bundled Node 20
- Ignore engines warnings that mention Node 20.18.x

## Project pin

- Prefer Node **24** (see `.nvmrc` and CI `node-version: 24`)
- If the nvm patch version changes, update the PATH prefix to the installed `v24.*` under `~/.nvm/versions/node/`
